merged.untrustedBody:
The six waves of workers that landed 521 functions in `src/` (PRs #149, #151, #153, #155, #156 and #159) left attempts that did not match at every place. `AGENTS.md` and `docs/AGENT_WORKFLOW.md` say what a bounded attempt leaves behind: its C in `nonmatching/<area>/<func>.c`, the `INCLUDE_ASM` marker back in `src/`, and a line in the README saying how far it got and what was tried. This branch does that, instead of leaving the attempts in a scratch directory.

- 154 files under `nonmatching/levels/` and `nonmatching/game/`, each with the worker's own note at the top and the closest C below it;
- six bodies that are exact but that the build refuses (`needs .rodata at its place, which is not C`), listed with the bodies that link at some of their places only, the way `func_L00_002B1308` already was;
- one attempt per function: the nine functions the earlier Haiku trial had already preserved are left untouched;
- a new README section, "Level functions from the six agent waves (2026-10-12)"

